"""The web UI: a page in the operator's browser that talks to the broker (`social_data_pipeline.control.broker`) through its socket, and does nothing else.

It runs in a container that holds only the broker's socket folder and its own certificate (`sdp webui start`, see `social_data_pipeline.webui_host`); every action goes through the broker's typed verbs. It has the login, the Overview and the Management pages (Sources, Databases, Runs, System), from which an action is chosen, shown with its `sdp` command and run once it is confirmed.

Modules: `config` (the settings the container is started with), `guard` (the checks every request passes and the headers every response gets), `sessions` (the browser sessions, kept in memory only), `limiter` (failed logins per client address), `words` (the broker's error codes as sentences), `cleaning` (text from programs made fit to show), `overview` (the Overview's data), `pages` (the data of the other Management pages), `actions` (the table of what the pages may ask the broker, and `call`, through which every request but the login and the logout goes), `work` (a session's pending actions, outcomes and output views), `output` (the output view of a run), `calls` (the bounds on broker calls), `management` (the routes of the Management pages and of the actions), `app` (the application and its other routes), `probe` (asks the broker for `hello` from inside the container). `config`, `words`, `cleaning`, `limiter`, `sessions`, `overview`, `pages`, `actions`, `work`, `output` and `probe` use the standard library and the broker's client only; `calls` also anyio; `guard`, `management` and `app` also FastAPI, Starlette and Jinja2. Nothing here imports the CLI, the registry or PyYAML: the container has none of them.
"""
